positions.description:
◆ Investigate and solve the root cause of a multitude of technical issues as well as answering questions regarding upgrades, installations, and other software/hardware/network problems;
◆ Some of the technologies used include: Active Directory, Software Center, Citrix, Cisco AnyConnect, RSA, Avaya and various internal systems testing, network management and account management tools;
◆ Effectively utilize resources including: internally created tools, knowledge base articles, technical expertise of coworkers and resources such as  SCCM, user admin, and other related tools;
◆ Clearly and thoroughly document troubleshooting and various queries in Service Now, and monitor incidents from initial occurrence to resolution/escalation;
◆ Monitor multiple location outage reports and dispatch the appropriate staff to resolve when necessary;
◆ Communicate with internal team via Slack and Microsoft Outlook;
◆ Attend regularly scheduled meetings to adhere to most effective and up to date technical resolution techniques;

◆ The initial contact for reporting technical issues, and answering questions regarding upgrades, installations, and other software/hardware/network issues for numerous law firms;
◆ Effectively implement the steps found in available resources while using a variety of different remote access, user admin, and related tools depending on the specific law firm;
◆ Some of the technologies used include: Active Directory, Software Center,  Microsoft Exchange, VMWare, Citrix, ServiceNow, IQTrack, Bomgar, iManage etc. ;
◆ Clearly and thoroughly document requests for assistance in Service Now through to resolution/escalation;
◆ Managed a multitude of Desktop Farms/Machines using VMWare Horizon Admin Console.

